; the property of returning to original shape after deformation.
; elastic: deformation is reversible. energy stored and returned.
; inelastic (plastic): deformation is permanent. energy dissipated.
; 
; the numeric measure: coefficient of restitution e (0 to 1).
; e = 1: perfectly elastic. e = 0: perfectly inelastic.
; 
; at the molecular level:
; elastic: bonds stretch and return. springs, polymer chains.
; inelastic: bonds break or rearrange. clay, putty, metals under large stress.
; 
; Hooke's law: F = -kx. valid within the elastic limit.
; beyond elastic limit: yield point → plastic deformation → fracture.
; 
; everyday: rubber elastic (e≈0.8). clay inelastic (e≈0). glass brittle.

(kosha elasticity
  (vishesa common-sense-varga materials-varga)
  (swarupa subanta)
  (yukta coefficient-of-restitution spring-force collision-varga))
